  "preamble": "Change of a palatalized voiced labial stop [bʲ] into a voiced alveolo-palatal fricative [ʑ]. The labial closure is lost and the palatal glide becomes a fricative, probably through an affricate stage [dʑ]. In the East Bodish language Dzala, Proto-Bodish *bʲ appears as zh-, while the closely related Kurtöp and Khengkha have the affricate j-.",
